<task id="167" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>The every-route authorization guard (owner round 9 item 3): extend task 074's RouteAuthorizationGuardTests so EVERY BFF route file is governed and every route declares a per-resource check, an admin policy, or a reasoned waiver; the 82 sweep findings (90 route keys) start as Pending waivers owned by their fix tasks 159-166</title>
    <phase>Session 27, owner round 9 (2026-10-03): the route authorization sweep</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies tests/** (root CLAUDE.md §8 TEST-MODIFYING override: code-review + adr-check run unconditionally). The guard decides which BFF routes the build accepts as authorized; a false "gated" verdict hides a disclosure.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security forcing function over 120 files and 431 registrations. Each route's credit is a judgment (which filter really decides, which handler really checks, which data is really the caller's own), and the guard itself must fail closed on every parse it cannot complete.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs, which tasks 159-166 also edit (each deletes its own Pending waivers and adds credit for its fixed routes). By owner decision (round 9 item 2) it runs at the same time as 159-166 on its own branch; the main session reconciles the waiver list at integration. It changes no file under src/, so it touches none of the project's parallel-unsafe zones (Api/ExternalAccess/**, Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**, Spaarke.Core/Auth/**, DataverseWebApiService.cs); it only reads them.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>testing, security, auth, archtest, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner round 9 item 3 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md, "Owner answers, round 9"): "every BFF route must declare how it is authorized: a record-level check, an admin policy, or an explicit, reasoned waiver for a route that only touches the caller's own data. A new route with only a sign-in check fails the build. It extends task 074's RouteAuthorizationGuardTests to every route file. The 82 known findings start as Pending waivers owned by their fix tasks; the guard's stale-waiver rule then forces each fix to delete its waiver." Evidence: notes/route-authorization-sweep-2026-10-02.md (82 confirmed findings, 6 refuted, 62 noteworthy, from workflow run wf_c2daa097-2f4).</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Today the route guard (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs) checks only the 25 files in its GovernedFiles list. It credits any filter whose name contains "AuthorizationFilter", and it lets whole files skip the per-route rule as "HandlerAuthorized". The 2026-10-02 sweep found 82 routes where a signed-in caller acts, as the BFF's own identity, on a record it has no rights to. Most of them sit in files the guard never reads, or behind filters it credits that decide nothing. Extend the guard so that every route in every BFF endpoint file shows one of four things: a per-resource decision the guard can see, a verified in-handler decision, an admin policy on a pinned operator route, or a written waiver. Record the 82 findings as Pending waivers owned by tasks 159-166, so the build stays green while they are fixed and each fix must delete its waiver. Change no product code.</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-03, owner rounds 9-10" binding="true">
    <!-- Read these before step 0. Each overrides anything below that contradicts it. -->
    <amendment>Owner decisions now run to round 10: re-read notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md rounds 9 and 10 on work/unified-access-control-r2 before step 0. They are newer than this POML.</amendment>
    <amendment>Tasks 159-166 run IN PARALLEL with you and do NOT touch your ledger or waivers. They record a "Route authorization ledger input" table in their notes, and the main session fills ResolvedBy and ProofTest from those at integration. Do not wait for them, and do not depend on their branches.</amendment>
    <amendment>Task 159's events list (GET /api/v1/events) will be a "query runs as the caller" HandlerDecision, not a Permanent waiver. Leave room for that shape.</amendment>
    <amendment>Do not stop on the number of UNOWNED-NEW candidates. Record each as a Pending waiver owned by "UNOWNED-NEW", with a one-line reason, and list them all in the note. The main session assigns them after you finish. Escalation trigger 8 is answered by this instruction.</amendment>
    <amendment>Owner round 10 item 1 (dead routes) is the fix tasks' job. Do not delete routes here.</amendment>
