  <role>SPAARKE platform developer: structural fitness functions over the BFF source (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests, ADR-038 Amendment A1 KEEP path), ASP.NET Core Minimal API route registration (ADR-001, ADR-008 endpoint filters), and the BFF's authorization seams (ADR-003 fail closed).</role>

  <goal>When this task is done:
(1) Every file the census finds is classified in GovernedFiles, and the GovernedFiles set equals the census set exactly. The census is EndpointFiles(): every non-obj/bin .cs file under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ containing a route registration (Map{Verb}, MapMethods or MapHealthChecks). There were 120 files at authoring, 3 of them outside Api/**.
(2) The scanner resolves every registration to its FULL route key (verb plus absolute path). This includes MapMethods (including the collection-expression form ["PATCH"]), MapHealthChecks, a path given as a same-file const, and routes registered on a group that another file declares (aggregator binding). A registration it cannot resolve is a violation, never a skip. No two registrations produce the same key.
(3) Rule A applies to every route in every governed file. A route passes only with one of these:
- a credited per-resource filter;
- a ResourceAccessRequirement policy (the existing PolicyOnlyRoutes pin);
- a verified HandlerDecision declaration;
- an admin mechanism on a route in the pinned AdminOnlyRoutes set;
- a Permanent waiver with a stated basis;
- a Pending waiver with an owning task.
The file-level HandlerAuthorized exemption is gone.
(4) Rule A credits filters only by an explicit allow-list of attachment forms that were read and found to decide. The pass-through shapes the sweep found are NOT credited: AnalysisAuthorizationFilter in AnalysisAccess mode, CommunicationAuthorizationFilter, AiAuthorizationFilter, DataverseAuthorizationFilter in FromRouteValueWithRecord and FromFetchXmlBody modes, TenantAuthorizationFilter, and the identity-only filters. Each sits in NonDecidingAttachments with an owning task, and a pin test fails when its pass-through is removed from source, so the entry is reclassified when its filter is fixed. Every attachment form used on any route is classified in exactly one list, and an unclassified form fails the build.
(5) Rule B (NoAuthorizationFilterIsDecorative), the census and fail-closed parsing are kept and extended to every credited filter. Decision-service tokens now match whole identifiers, so "IAiAuthorizationService" no longer satisfies the "AuthorizationService" token by substring.
(6) All 90 route keys of the 82 sweep findings are Pending waivers with OwningTask 159-166 per the ledger below. They are recorded in a pinned sweep ledger that forbids a Permanent waiver on any of them. An entry resolves only by credit plus a named proof test.
(7) Every route the extended guard flags that the sweep did not confirm is one of two things. Either it is a Permanent waiver whose basis was verified by reading the handler, or it is a Pending waiver owned by "UNOWNED-NEW" and listed in the task note for the main session to assign. Nothing is silently waived.
(8) The guard suite is green on the branch. Every new rule has a negative control (fires on a seeded violation) and a positive control (does not fire on the sanctioned shape).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Every anchor below was read on the work tree at b18a7d321 (branch work/unified-access-control-r2, 2026-10-02). Line numbers drift: re-verify each before relying on it.

THE GUARD TODAY (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs, 2289 lines).
- Scope enum: :104-122 (RouteLevelGate, HandlerAuthorized, GroupGated).
- GovernedFiles: :126-343 (25 files). Every other file is "NotGoverned" (:99-101), so Rule A never looks at it.
- Waivers: :378-684. The record is Waiver(Route, Kind, OwningTask, Reason) at :376; the kinds Pending/Permanent are at :370-374; the maintenance procedure is at :348-368.
  - Eight Permanent waivers are live today and no Pending ones: PUT /api/obo/me/files/{*path} :515 (owner "076"), POST /api/v1/documents :573, GET /api/v1/documents :578, the three /api/office/communications routes :618, :628, :635, GET /api/office/search/entities :654, GET /api/office/search/matter-types :665.
- PolicyOnlyRoutes :692-709 (empty, pinned); ResourcePolicies :718-732.
- Census:
  - ExpectedEndpointFileCount = 120 at :875 (a count only, not the set), with its history comment :734-874.
  - TheEndpointFileCensusIsPinned :1350-1389.
- Rules:
  - Rule A: :881-934 (RouteLevelGate files only).
  - Waiver reason/owner rule: :936-985.
  - NoWaiverIsStale :987-1061 (a Pending waiver on a now-Filter route is stale; any waiver on an absent route is stale).
  - Policy-only pin :1063-1100.
- Rule B, NoAuthorizationFilterIsDecorative :1106-1182:
  - The subject is a file named *AuthorizationFilter.cs, or one in ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames.
  - Each must contain a DecisionServices token (:1274-1296, matched by SUBSTRING via string.Contains at :1129), or every endpoint file attaching it must.
  - ClaimOnlyFilters :1194-1241; KnownDecorativeFilters :1267 (empty).
- Rule E, GroupGatedFilesRegisterNoAbsolutePaths :1302-1348: it regex-scans every Map{Verb} literal in a GroupGated file.
- Controls:
  - Detector_NegativeControl_FiresOnEachHistoricalMiss :1395-1489.
  - RuleB_NegativeControl_FiresOnADecorativeFilter :1491-1559.
  - Detector_PositiveControl_DoesNotFireOnGatedRoutes :1561-1614. Its fixtures use .AddEndpointFilter&lt;BulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter&gt;() and .AddEndpointFilter&lt;EntityAccessFilter&gt;(); NEITHER is the form the real code uses (see "credit" below).
  - The Office baseline control :1616-1643; the Office positive control :1645-1671.
  - RuleBCoversEveryFilterRuleACredits :1673-1703; the nested-group control :1705-1735.
  - Scanner completeness :1737-1825, which pins OBOEndpoints.cs at 3 registrations.
- Machinery:
  - MapCall regex :1851 matches only Map(Get|Post|Put|Patch|Delete).
  - GroupDecl :1862 matches only `var x = y.MapGroup("literal")`.
  - ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames :1886-1896.
  - FilterMarker :1898-1902 credits ANY ".Add*AuthorizationFilter(" or ".AddEndpointFilter&lt;*Authorization*Filter|*Access*Filter&gt;", plus four explicit names.
  - NamedPolicy :1904 matches string-literal policies only.
  - Scan :1926-2029 resolves receivers by variable NAME within one file.
  - EndpointFiles :2229-2235 covers the whole BffRoot, not only Api/, but selects files by MapCall only.

WHY THE GUARD MISSED THE SWEEP'S FINDINGS (each verified at authoring).
(a) Coverage. Of the 120 census files only 25 are governed. Rule A never ran over Events, Dataverse, Communication, Ai (except search/visualization), Memory, Insights, Workspace, Reporting, SpeAdmin (except ContainerItemEndpoints), Admin, FieldMappings, WorkAssignmentEndpoints or EndpointMappingExtensions.
(b) File-level exemption. The eight Compose files and the two external data files are HandlerAuthorized, so Rule A skips them. Sweep findings S-63, S-64, S-65 and S-80 sit in Compose files.
(c) Decorative credit. FilterMarker credits each of these attachments, yet each lets the request through without a record decision:
  - .AddAnalysisRecordAuthorizationFilter() runs AnalysisAuthorizationFilter in AuthorizationMode.AnalysisAccess.
    - AuthorizeAnalysisAccessAsync (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs:185-212) parses analysisId and returns next(context) with no lookup ("TRACKED: GitHub #233", :203).
    - Rule B passes the file because it contains "IAiAuthorizationService", which contains the DecisionServices token "AuthorizationService" as a substring.
    - The sibling .AddAnalysisExecuteAuthorizationFilter() (:19-29; DocumentAccess mode :121-174, which 400s on zero ids and 403s on deny) DOES decide.
  - .AddEndpointFilter&lt;CommunicationAuthorizationFilter&gt;() (Api/Filters/CommunicationAuthorizationFilter.cs, 43 lines; next at :41) checks IsAuthenticated and an oid, nothing else.
    - It is in ClaimOnlyFilters with a reason (:1211-1215) saying that per-record scoping is done by ICommunicationAccessFilter.
    - The sweep shows that is false for send, archive, suggest-associations, create-task, threads, confirm-affinity, proposals and accounts/verify.
  - .AddAiAuthorizationFilter() and .AddEndpointFilter&lt;AiAuthorizationFilter&gt;() (Api/Filters/AiAuthorizationFilter.cs).
    - It decides only for arguments of type DocumentAnalysisRequest, IEnumerable&lt;DocumentAnalysisRequest&gt; or Guid (:130-153), and otherwise returns next (:84).
    - At authoring, none of its 46 attachment sites binds DocumentAnalysisRequest. The only one binding a Guid, GET /api/ai/chat/sessions/by-analysis/{analysisId:guid}, binds an ANALYSIS id that the filter authorizes as a DOCUMENT id. So it decides for no route in this codebase.
    - Rule B passes it through the same substring.
  - .AddDataverseAuthorizationFilter(EntitySource.FromRouteValueWithRecord) and (EntitySource.FromFetchXmlBody) (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/DataverseAuthorizationFilter.cs).
    - ResolveEntities (:177-193) handles FromRouteValueWithRecord in the SAME branch as FromRouteValue and returns only the entity logical name. :128-148 checks only an entity-level Read privilege through IDataversePrivilegeChecker.
    - That is a correct decision for SCHEMA routes (EntitySource.FromRouteValue: GET /api/dataverse/metadata/{entityLogicalName}, GET /api/dataverse/gridconfigurations/{entityLogicalName}, GET /api/dataverse/savedqueries/{entityLogicalName}).
    - It is no decision for the record and FetchXML routes (S-10, S-09).
    - EntitySource.FromSavedQueryEntity exists in the enum (:21) but no route uses it.
  - .AddTenantAuthorizationFilter() (Api/Filters/TenantAuthorizationFilter.cs).
    - It compares the tid claim with a tenant id found in the request (:73-94), and passes through when none is found (:76-81). It never consults a record.
    - It is ClaimOnly (:1197-1199), which is correct about what it decides. The defect is that Rule A credits it as a per-resource gate on the RAG routes (S-04, S-05, S-06, S-30).
  - Identity-only filters credited the same way:
    - .AddEndpointFilter&lt;WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter&gt;() (Api/Filters/WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter.cs, oid only).
    - .AddAgentAuthorizationFilter() (Api/Agent/AgentAuthorizationFilter.cs, oid+tid only). Its ClaimOnly reason (:1207-1210) says it "serves no document metadata", which S-18 and S-19 disprove.
    - .AddCallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter() (Api/Filters/CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter.cs: principal resolution, a precondition for the handler's check).
    - .AddReportingAuthorizationFilter() (Api/Reporting/ReportingAuthorizationFilter.cs: a module role claim; not per-resource and not an operator surface).
    - .AddSpeAdminTenantScopeFilter() (tenant scope). It passes through when no configId is present (Api/Filters/SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter.cs:76-78), and SpeAdminTenantScope.CanAccessConfigAsync returns true on a lookup error and for a BU-less config (Services/SpeAdmin/SpeAdminTenantScope.cs:99-122).
(d) Real filters the guard does NOT credit today, because their names lack "Authorization":
  - .AddSessionOwnershipFilter() (Api/Filters/SessionOwnershipFilter.cs:87-97). It compares owners through ChatSessionManager and answers 404 for a missing or not-owned session. It refuses rather than passes when the route has no {sessionId}.
  - .AddDelegationRuleFilter() (Api/ExternalAccess/DelegationRuleFilter.cs). It checks Write on the target via CallerRecordAccessProbe (:37, :86-184), and every exit denies 403.
  Both must become credited per-resource filters, inspected by Rule B. SessionOwnershipFilter consults no DecisionServices token (ChatSessionManager), so it needs an OWNER-COMPARISON ClaimOnly entry, like JobOwnershipFilter at :1228-1236.
(e) Real attachment forms the allow-list must spell exactly (grep at authoring):
  - BulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter is attached as .AddBulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter() (Api/DocumentsBulkEndpoints.cs:65), NOT .AddEndpointFilter&lt;BulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter&gt;.
  - EntityAccessFilter is attached as .AddEntityAccessFilter().
  - Inline lambdas attach with a bare .AddEndpointFilter(async (context, next) =&gt; ...). The one route-level instance is the Guid.Empty validator at Api/Office/OfficeEndpoints.cs:1496, which is validation, not authorization.
  - The webhook HMAC is attached as .RequireWebhookSignature(...) (Api/Filters/WebhookSignatureFilter.cs:252; used at Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs:402 and Api/ComposeSyncEndpoints.cs:44).
(f) Parser gaps.
  - Three routes register with MapMethods using the collection-expression form ["PATCH"]: Api/Ai/ChatEndpoints.cs:141 PATCH /sessions/{sessionId}/context (sweep S-23), :154 PATCH /sessions/{sessionId}, :213 PATCH /sessions/{sessionId}/tabs.
  - Two register with MapHealthChecks: Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:59 /healthz and :66 /healthz/catalog.
  - Two take their path from a const, so their registrations are unparseable today:
    - Endpoints/Diagnostics/TenantContainerResolverEndpoint.cs: const at :79, MapGet at :106, giving GET /api/diagnostics/tenant-container-resolver.
    - Endpoints/Onboarding/ConsentCallbackEndpoint.cs: const at :45, MapPost at :70, giving POST /api/onboarding/consent-callback.
  - About 120 routes in 39 files are registered on a RouteGroupBuilder passed in from an aggregator, so today the scanner keys them as fragments ("POST /configs"). The aggregators:
    - Api/SpeAdminEndpoints.cs:27-35: /api/spe + RequireAuthorization + AddSpeAdminAuthorizationFilter + AddSpeAdminTenantScopeFilter.
      - It binds 19 child files in Api/SpeAdmin/ in TWO call forms: the extension form `group.MapConfigEndpoints()` and the static form `ContainerEndpoints.MapContainerEndpoints(group)`.
      - Child files nest further groups (ConfigEndpoints.cs "/configs", DashboardEndpoints.cs, SecurityEndpoints.cs).
    - Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs:30-47: /api/compose + RequireAuthorization, binding 8 Compose files.
      - MapComposeSyncEndpoints(routes) also receives the ROOT builder. Its webhook POST /api/compose/webhooks/spe-doc-changed is registered on `routes` with an ABSOLUTE path (Api/ComposeSyncEndpoints.cs:42), AllowAnonymous + RequireWebhookSignature.
    - Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:54-57: externalGroup /api/v1/external + RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.ExternalCollaboration) + AddCallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter.
      - It binds ExternalProjectDataEndpoints (17 routes) and ExternalModuleDataEndpoints, which nests `externalGroup.MapGroup("/api/dataverse")`.
      - That gives FIVE routes: POST /api/v1/external/api/dataverse/fetch, GET .../record/{entityLogicalName}/{id:guid}, GET .../metadata/{entityLogicalName}, GET .../savedquery/{savedQueryId:guid}, GET .../savedqueries/{entityLogicalName}.
    - The same file at :123-126: adminGroup /api/v1/external-access + RequireAuthorization + AddDelegationRuleFilter, binding 10 files plus the inline close-project route at :158.
  - ⚠️ KEY COLLISION HAZARD. Without the aggregator prefix, ExternalModuleDataEndpoints produces "POST /api/dataverse/fetch" and "GET /api/dataverse/record/{entityLogicalName}/{id:guid}". Those are EXACTLY the keys of sweep findings S-09 and S-10 in Api/Dataverse/. A Pending waiver written for S-09 would then silently cover a different route, and NoWaiverIsStale would compare the wrong routes.
(g) Dead registration. Api/ExternalAccess/ProjectClosureEndpoint.cs:46 MapProjectClosureEndpoint has zero callers (grep at authoring); the live route is mapped inline at ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:158. Scanned naively, it produces a duplicate "POST /api/v1/external-access/close-project" key. It is the ONLY duplicate key once aggregator prefixes are applied (checked at authoring).
(h) Admin policies.
  - RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin"): the policy is at Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs:362-377; it is used in Api/Admin/JobsEndpoints.cs:53, Api/Admin/MembershipAdminEndpoints.cs:46 and Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs:162.
  - RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.RagApiKey): the policy is at :328-332; it is used at RagEndpoints.cs:142 (service automation key).
  - .AddSpeAdminAuthorizationFilter(): on /api/spe, and in Api/Insights/PrecedentAdminEndpoints.cs.
  - .AddRegistrationAuthorizationFilter(): Api/RegistrationEndpoints.cs approve/reject.
  - RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.ExternalCollaboration) only selects authentication schemes. It is NOT an admin mechanism.
  - There is no DefaultPolicy or FallbackPolicy, so a bare RequireAuthorization() means "signed in".
  - ⚠️ The SystemAdmin assertion also passes any token whose scope claim CONTAINS the substring "admin" (:371-373). This is recorded as a note for the main session, not fixed here.
(i) A route the sweep did not cover: GET /healthz/dataverse/doc/{id}. The sweep traced Api/** only.
  - The route is at Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:81-111. It is AllowAnonymous and mapped unconditionally; its only control is the "anonymous" rate limit.
  - It reads a caller-chosen sprk_document app-only through IDocumentDataverseService, and returns its name, file name, parent document, matter, project and invoice ids.
  - ⚠️ It has a named CONSUMER: .claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md:50 (§9c, the post-deploy "MI → Dataverse" smoke check), plus the runbooks projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/slot-swap-runbook.md and 051-operator-runbook.md. Whoever fixes it must first move that smoke check to the id-less sibling /healthz/dataverse (:74). This task only records this.
  - Its siblings take no id: /healthz/dataverse (:74) and /healthz/dataverse/crud (:77, a top-1 read).
(j) POST /api/v1/documents binds CreateDocumentRequest (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs: `required string ContainerId` from the body; OwningTeamId is [JsonIgnore]). So the request NAMES an existing resource, the destination container. Today's Permanent waiver at :573 ("CREATE. There is no pre-existing resource") is therefore not true as written. The sweep's S-36 chain names this route as step 1.

ROUTE COUNT AT AUTHORING. These figures come from an independent Python approximation of the scanner over the work tree, with the aggregator prefixes applied.
