THE SWEEP'S SIX REFUTED ROUTES, and how the extended guard sees them.
- POST /api/finance/matters/{matterId}/recalculate and POST /api/finance/projects/{projectId}/recalculate: credited by FinanceAuthorizationFilter (task 130). No waiver.
- POST /api/v1/external-access/revoke: credited by the adminGroup's DelegationRuleFilter. No waiver.
- GET /api/reporting/reports: refuted only because of the Reporting role filter, which this task does NOT credit. It is flagged. Classify it by reading the handler: Permanent ReferenceData only if it lists a configured catalog and nothing caller-chosen; otherwise UNOWNED-NEW.
- GET /api/ai/chat/context-mappings/analysis/{analysisId} (Api/Ai/AnalysisChatContextEndpoints.cs:37). The skeptic found it fails safe only because the app-only Retrieve asks for attributes that do not exist (Services/Ai/Chat/AnalysisChatContextResolver.cs:267-277). That is not an authorization decision. It is flagged; record it as Pending UNOWNED-NEW (a latent IDOR), not Permanent.
- GET /api/ai/playbooks/runs/{runId:guid}, /stream, /detail and POST .../cancel (Api/Ai/PlaybookRunEndpoints.cs:56-95).
  - The sweep refuted these because PlaybookOrchestrationService is Scoped (Infrastructure/DI/AnalysisServicesModule.cs:1302) and _activeRuns is an instance field (Services/Ai/PlaybookOrchestrationService.cs:61), so another caller's run is never reachable.
  - Re-verify. If it holds, record Permanent CallerScopedOnly citing both anchors, and note to the main session that these routes can then never find a run started by an earlier request (a functional defect). If it does not hold, record UNOWNED-NEW.

PRELIMINARY CLASSIFICATION of the uncredited, non-sweep routes. This is the author's reading at authoring. The executor MUST read each handler and decide. The categories are the PermanentBasis values defined in the constraints.
- Anonymous at authoring (16 routes). Each needs Permanent AnonymousByDesign, and the reason must name the compensating control and its file:line; otherwise UNOWNED-NEW.
