  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the whole task. Change NO file under src/. Change no client code, script, Dataverse or Azure resource either. The deliverable is the ArchTest guard, its data, and the task note. If a registration cannot be parsed without reformatting product code, fix the scanner. If the scanner cannot be made to parse it, fire escalation trigger 3. Do not fix any finding here: the fixes are tasks 159-166.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: the guard's own decisions. Fail closed. Each of the following is a VIOLATION, never a skip or a pass:
- an unparseable registration;
- an unresolved route path or group prefix;
- a GroupGated file whose aggregator binding cannot be found;
- two registrations producing the same route key;
- a HandlerDecision whose handler or hop method cannot be located, or whose hop resolves to more than one body without the seam in every body;
- an unknown PermanentBasis;
- an attachment form used on a route that no classification list names;
- a file the census finds that GovernedFiles does not list.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: census and scanner.
- EndpointFiles() selects a file by the SAME registration vocabulary the scanner reads: Map{Verb}, MapMethods and MapHealthChecks. A future file registering only MapMethods must be counted.
- Aggregator binding resolves both call forms, `group.MapXEndpoints()` and `XEndpoints.MapXEndpoints(group)`, from the aggregator's source. The aggregator files Api/SpeAdminEndpoints.cs and Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs register no route directly and are not census files; they are read as aggregators. The bound group's prefix and chain are inherited, including nested groups inside the child file.
- A registration on a SECOND, root builder parameter (MapComposeSyncEndpoints's `routes`) is a root registration. Its key is its literal path and its chain is its own.
- Rule E (GroupGatedFilesRegisterNoAbsolutePaths) applies only to registrations on the aggregator-bound group parameter. It must not flag the Compose webhook on `routes`.
- MapMethods verbs are read from the collection-expression form ["PATCH"], the new[] { "PATCH" } form and the new string[] { ... } form. Any other form is unparseable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: credit.
- Replace FilterMarker's generic "contains Authorization/Access" alternations with an explicit allow-list of credited per-resource attachment forms, one entry per form.
- Each entry carries the filter file and a written reason of at least 60 characters naming what the filter checks and where (file:line).
- The allow-list at authoring (verify each by reading the filter):
  - .AddDocumentAuthorizationFilter(...), .AddContainerDocumentAuthorizationFilter(), .AddBulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter();
  - .AddRecordSearchAuthorizationFilter(), .AddSemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter(), .AddVisualizationAuthorizationFilter(), .AddVisualizationContentAuthorizationFilter();
  - .AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter(...), .AddRecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter(...);
  - .AddEntityAccessFilter(), .AddJobOwnershipFilter(), .AddTodoSourceAccessFilter(), .AddQuickCreateSourceAccessFilter(), .AddOfficeVersionSaveAuthorizationFilter();
  - .AddPlaybookAccessAuthorizationFilter(), .AddPlaybookOwnerAuthorizationFilter();
  - .AddSessionOwnershipFilter() (new), .AddDelegationRuleFilter() (new);
  - .AddAnalysisExecuteAuthorizationFilter() (and NOT .AddAnalysisRecordAuthorizationFilter());
  - .AddDataverseAuthorizationFilter(EntitySource.FromRouteValue ...) only.
- Do not list a form no route uses (FromSavedQueryEntity, .AddEndpointFilter&lt;BulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter&gt;, .AddEndpointFilter&lt;EntityAccessFilter&gt;). A test fails on an allow-list entry that no route attaches.
- Rule A and Rule B both derive from this one list: keep the "one list, two consumers" property (:1880-1885). Each credited filter's file is inspected by Rule B.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the attachment-form census. Every authorization-shaped call that appears in any route chain (route or group level) must be named in exactly ONE of these lists:
- the credited allow-list;
- the four admin mechanisms;
- NonDecidingAttachments;
- a NotAuthorization list. Each NotAuthorization entry carries a reason. At authoring it holds .AddOfficeAuthFilter, .AddOfficeRateLimitFilter, .AddIdempotencyFilter, .AddTenantEnvironmentRoutingFilter, .AddEndpointFilter&lt;DocumentUrlIdentityFilter&gt;, the inline .AddEndpointFilter(async ...) lambda, .RequireWebhookSignature(...), .RequireRateLimiting(...), .RequireAuthorization() and .RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.ExternalCollaboration).
"Authorization-shaped" means any .Add*Filter call, any .AddEndpointFilter call, any .RequireAuthorization call, and .RequireWebhookSignature. A form in none of the lists fails the build naming the file:line, so the next new filter must be classified before it can merge. A form in two lists fails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: non-credited forms.
- Record each known pass-through as a NonDecidingAttachments entry with:
  - the attachment form;
  - the filter file;
  - the reason;
  - the source evidence;
  - an OwningTask — the fix task whose POML modifies that filter: AnalysisRecord mode 162, AiAuthorizationFilter 164, CommunicationAuthorizationFilter 161, DataverseAuthorizationFilter record/fetch modes 160, TenantAuthorizationFilter 163, AgentAuthorizationFilter 164, SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter 165, or "-" for a filter that is an identity or role precondition by design: WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter, CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter, ReportingAuthorizationFilter.
- Pin each entry's evidence with a test that reads the filter source and asserts that the pass-through still exists:
  - AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizeAnalysisAccessAsync returns next without a decision-service call;
  - AiAuthorizationFilter returns next when no document id is extracted, and no endpoint handler binds DocumentAnalysisRequest;
  - CommunicationAuthorizationFilter references no decision service;
  - DataverseAuthorizationFilter.ResolveEntities handles FromRouteValueWithRecord in the FromRouteValue branch, returning the entity name only and never reading the record id, and returns entity names only for FromFetchXmlBody;
  - TenantAuthorizationFilter passes through when no tenant is found;
  - WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter, AgentAuthorizationFilter and CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter reference no decision service;
  - ReportingAuthorizationFilter decides from role claims;
  - SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter passes through without a configId.
- When a pin fails because a filter was fixed, the failure message gives this remedy: delete the NonDecidingAttachments entry, add the form to the credited allow-list if it now decides, and re-run Rule A.
- Correct the ClaimOnlyFilters reasons for CommunicationAuthorizationFilter (:1211-1215) and AgentAuthorizationFilter (:1207-1210). They must no longer claim that per-record scoping happens elsewhere, or that the agent gateway serves no document data.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: Rule B's decision vocabulary.
- DecisionServices and CallerContextSeams tokens match WHOLE identifiers (an identifier boundary on both sides, outside comments), not substrings. Add "IAiAuthorizationService" as its own DecisionServices entry, with a reason naming AnalysisAuthorizationFilter's DocumentAccess path (:139).
- Re-run Rule B and record in the note every filter whose verdict changed. Add a token only after reading that the filter calls it. A filter that fails only because it relied on a substring match is either given its real token with a reason, or reported (escalation trigger 5).
- Keep the RuleB_NegativeControl prose control passing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: admin credit.
- Exactly four mechanisms count as an admin policy:
  - RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin");
  - RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.RagApiKey);
  - .AddSpeAdminAuthorizationFilter() (including when inherited from the /api/spe aggregator);
  - .AddRegistrationAuthorizationFilter().
- ReportingAuthorizationFilter is a module role gate, not admin. RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.ExternalCollaboration) is scheme selection, not admin.
- A route credited ONLY by an admin mechanism must be in a pinned AdminOnlyRoutes set. Copy TheSetOfPolicyOnlyRoutesIsPinned, so that both "added" and "removed" fail. Group the set by file, with one written reason per group stating why the surface is an operator surface.
- A route that also carries a credited per-resource filter is per-resource, not admin-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: HandlerDecision.
- A route whose decision is in its handler is credited only by a per-route declaration with these fields:
  - the route key;
  - the handler method name in the endpoint file;
  - the decision seam;
  - an optional chain of up to two "ConcreteType.Method" hops the handler calls;
  - a reason citing file:line.
- The test locates the handler body: the method by name, or the inline lambda in the registration statement. It follows each declared hop to that method's body, finding the single file under src/server/** (excluding obj/bin) that declares the concrete type. That covers Spaarke.Core and Spaarke.Dataverse as well as the BFF. The test passes only when the last body contains the seam token outside comments.
- An interface type in a hop is refused (name the implementation). If a method name has several overloads in the type, every overload must contain the seam.
- The seam must be in DecisionServices, or in a new, separately listed CallerContextSeams vocabulary in which each entry has a reason and the type's file. Candidates to verify, all of which exist at authoring:
  - IDataverseUserClient (Infrastructure/Dataverse/IDataverseUserClient.cs);
  - IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery (Services/Communication/IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.cs);
  - DataverseImpersonation (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs);
  - CallerRecordAccessProbe (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs, already in DecisionServices);
  - the CallerPrincipal rights methods HoldsReadOnProject and RightsForRoot;
  - IsRecordAccessible;
  - Tier2ScopeFilterInjector (Api/ExternalAccess/Tier2ScopeFilterInjector.cs);
  - an OBO SPE call, only where SPE's check covers every caller-chosen id.
- Do not admit a general service type (this is the reason IOfficeService was refused, :1190-1192).
- A HandlerDecision is allowed only when the decision covers EVERY caller-chosen identifier the handler acts on. A decision that covers some of them is a finding, not a credit.
- State in the declaration list's maintenance comment that this is a PRESENCE check, the same limit Rule B has. The behavioural deny tests of tasks 159-166 are the proof, not this rule.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: waivers.
- Keep the Waiver record and its maintenance procedure, and add the following fields:
  - Permanent waivers carry a PermanentBasis from the closed set {AnonymousByDesign, CallerScopedOnly, ReferenceData, CreateWithNoPriorResource, CallerSuppliedContentOnly, OperatorGateInHandler}.
  - Pending waivers carry a Gap from {NoDecision, InsufficientDecision}.
  - An InsufficientDecision waiver carries ObservedMechanisms: the exact, normalized mechanism fingerprint of the route when the waiver was written. The fingerprint is built only from authorization-relevant forms: sorted distinct credited, admin and NonDeciding attachment names; "policy:NAME"; "anonymous"; and "handler:SEAM" for a HandlerDecision. NotAuthorization forms are excluded, so adding a rate limiter does not make a waiver stale.
- Definitions (each enforced by reading the handler; cite file:line in the reason):
  - CallerScopedOnly: the route reads or writes only rows keyed by a server-derived caller identity (oid, systemuserid, contact id), and takes no caller-chosen id of another principal's record.
  - ReferenceData: it returns configuration, catalog or schema content that is not customer record content, and takes no record id.
  - CreateWithNoPriorResource: the request names NO existing record, container, drive, owner, parent or regarding id.
  - CallerSuppliedContentOnly: it processes only bytes or text in the request and reads no stored record, index or file by any id.
  - AnonymousByDesign: the route is .AllowAnonymous(), and a MANDATORY compensating control is named with file:line. An optional control does not count.
  - OperatorGateInHandler: the handler denies every caller outside an operator allow-list or app-only classification before any data access.
- Pending waiver OwningTask values form a closed set: "159" through "166" and "UNOWNED-NEW". The existing Permanent owner strings ("076", "#1020", "#1021", "-") are kept.
- Never add a Permanent waiver to make the build green (maintenance rule 4, :362-363). Converting Permanent to Pending is allowed. Converting Pending to Permanent is forbidden; for sweep routes the ledger test enforces this, and elsewhere the reviewer enforces it.
- If no basis in the closed set fits a route that is genuinely safe, fire escalation trigger 2 rather than inventing a basis.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the sweep ledger.
- Add a pinned SweepFindings list with one entry per route key in the ledger above. Each entry holds: S-id, severity, route key, owning task, Gap, ResolvedBy = null, ProofTest = null.
- Owning task strings are exactly "159" through "166".
- The OwningTask and Gap of each sweep route's Pending waiver must equal the ledger's.
- The 82 findings and 90 route keys in the background are the closed set. Do not add, drop or re-own an entry. If a key cannot be found on the branch, fire escalation trigger 4.
- An entry resolves ONLY by credit. When ResolvedBy is set, the route must pass Rule A by a credited filter, a HandlerDecision or (for the admin-only SPE routes) its AdminOnlyRoutes entry, and it must carry NO waiver of any kind.
- ProofTest must then be set to "{repo-relative test file}::{test method name}", and the test asserts that the file exists and contains that method name. That test is the fix task's behavioural deny test.
- A fix task's "the query is the gate" shape (a list trimmed by an impersonated or delegated query) is recorded as a HandlerDecision, never as a Permanent waiver.
- State in the ledger's maintenance comment that for InsufficientDecision entries the guard cannot see a fix made inside an already-credited filter or handler. That resolution is by declaration (ResolvedBy plus ProofTest), reviewed at code review.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: fixes that landed before this task runs. If a 159-166 commit is already on this branch:
- Its fixed routes get no waiver. Their ledger entry has ResolvedBy set to that task and a ProofTest found in its commit.
- If that commit left a waiver on a sweep route (for example a Permanent "query is the gate" waiver), convert it to the credit form it describes (HandlerDecision), delete the waiver, and record the conversion in the note.
- If it cannot be expressed as a credit, fire escalation trigger 4.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: new findings.
- A route the extended guard flags that is not in the sweep ledger is a NEW finding, unless reading its handler proves it fits a PermanentBasis (cite file:line in the reason).
- Each NEW finding gets a Pending waiver with OwningTask "UNOWNED-NEW" and its Gap set honestly.
- Each NEW finding also gets a row in the task note: route key, file:line, what a signed-in or anonymous caller can do, proposed severity, evidence, and any named consumer a fix would break.
- Never waive a flagged route Permanent because it is inconvenient, and never omit one from the note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. These are source-analysis fitness functions on the ArchTests KEEP path (ADR-038 Amendment A1). Each rule carries a negative control and a positive control. The negative control fires on a seeded violation, ideally as an inline ScanText fixture so that it cannot go stale. The positive control does not fire on the sanctioned shape. Each rule's maintenance procedure lives in the test file (tests/CLAUDE.md).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: proof. Prove that every new rule bites by seeding:
- Make the violation locally on the REAL file. Where a real-file edit would touch src/, which is forbidden, use an inline fixture instead.
- Confirm that the rule fails naming the route, then restore.
- Record each proof (rule, what was seeded, the failure text) in the task note, as tasks 078 and 079 did (:569-570, :548-549).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: test runs (project hard gate, project CLAUDE.md "Hard gates"). Before the PR, run each of these in full and record pass/skip/fail counts:
- tests/Spaarke.ArchTests (NetArchTest included);
- the BFF unit suite, tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests;
- BOTH integration suites, tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests and tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests.
No test may make a Dataverse or Azure call. A failure outside this task's files is reported with its test name, not hidden.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: the whole task. Introduce no Dataverse plugins (none are possible in a test-only task). Do not suggest a plugin as a fix in any waiver reason or note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: the PR. This task changes no BFF source, so publish size and the CVE scan are unaffected; state that in the PR rather than measuring. Run /conflict-check before the PR: RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs is edited by tasks 159-166 and by other projects that add routes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 (binding)">Scope: the whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred. Scope discovered during execution is added to this task, or recorded as an UNOWNED-NEW waiver for the main session; it is not dropped. There is no live gate: this task makes no live call.</constraint>
  </constraints>

