    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="pinned route set" location="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:1063-1100">Compute the set from the scanner, compare it with a pinned literal set, and fail on both "added" and "removed".</pattern>
      <pattern name="filter/endpoint pair decides" location="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:1134-1162">A filter with no decision of its own passes only if every endpoint that attaches it consults a decision service. This is the shape for HandlerDecision's hop check.</pattern>
      <pattern name="self-liquidating waiver list" location="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:987-1061">A Pending waiver whose route gains a gate, or whose route disappears, fails; the remedy is deletion.</pattern>
      <pattern name="inline-fixture control" location="tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:1395-1489">Feed the scanner literal source text, so the negative control cannot go stale when real files change.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL (TEST-MODIFYING). Re-verify every anchor in the background on the current branch. Run the existing guard once and record its state. Check whether any of tasks 159-166 has already landed on this branch (git log for their task ids) and record which ones.</step>
    <step order="1">Scanner:
- Add MapMethods (all three verb-array forms), MapHealthChecks (as GET) and same-file const route paths.
- Add aggregator binding (both call forms, the second root-builder parameter, and nested groups in child files), verified against the aggregator's source.
- Add the duplicate-key check.
- Widen EndpointFiles() to the same vocabulary.
- Extend ScannerAccountsForEveryRegistrationInTheGovernedFiles's independent regex to the same forms.
- Classify the dead ProjectClosureEndpoint.MapProjectClosureEndpoint as NotMapped, with a zero-caller test, without deleting the file.</step>
    <step order="2">Census: classify every file EndpointFiles() returns into GovernedFiles (RouteLevelGate, GroupGated or NotMapped; retire the file-level HandlerAuthorized scope). Add a test that the GovernedFiles set equals the census set. Keep ExpectedEndpointFileCount and its history comment, with a new entry for this task.</step>
    <step order="3">Credit:
- Build the credited allow-list, the attachment-form census with NotAuthorization, NonDecidingAttachments with its owners and pins, the admin mechanisms with AdminOnlyRoutes, and HandlerDecision with CallerContextSeams.
- Define the AuthMechanism values they map to.
- Switch DecisionServices to whole-identifier matching and add IAiAuthorizationService.
- Update Rule B's inspected set to the allow-list. SessionOwnershipFilter and DelegationRuleFilter are now inspected; add an OWNER-COMPARISON ClaimOnly reason for SessionOwnershipFilter.
- Correct the two ClaimOnly reasons.
- Update the positive-control fixtures that use attachment forms the real code does not use.</step>
    <step order="4">Rule A over every route. Add the waiver fields (Basis, Gap, ObservedMechanisms), the extended stale rules, and the sweep ledger with its ResolvedBy and ProofTest test.</step>
    <step order="5">Classify every flagged route by reading its handler:
- The 90 sweep keys are Pending per the ledger.
- Every other flagged route is a verified Permanent basis, a verified HandlerDecision, or UNOWNED-NEW.
- Convert the GET /api/v1/documents Permanent waiver to Pending (S-66, owner 166). Re-verify POST /api/v1/documents under the strict CreateWithNoPriorResource definition.
- Report GET /healthz/dataverse/doc/{id} as soon as it is confirmed (escalation trigger 7), before finishing.</step>
    <step order="6">Write the controls and the seeding proofs for every new rule. Update the file's maintenance procedure text (the class summary, the scope boundary comment and the waiver maintenance procedure) to describe the every-route rule.</step>
    <step order="7">Run the four suites in full. Write the task note: scanner output counts, every UNOWNED-NEW finding, the not-flagged list for the main session, the Rule B verdict changes, the seeding proofs, and the landed-fix reconciliation. Update TASK-INDEX.md to ✅ [done].</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>1. A route whose intended audience is unclear (an operator surface or a user surface), so that you cannot decide between admin credit and a per-resource requirement: STOP for that route, list it with both readings, and continue with the rest. Do not credit it as admin by default.</trigger>
    <trigger>2. A flagged route that you are confident is safe but that fits none of the six PermanentBasis values: STOP and present the route and the proposed new basis with its definition, per CLAUDE.md §6. Do not widen an existing basis to cover it, and do not leave it unwaived.</trigger>
    <trigger>3. A registration the scanner cannot parse without changing a file under src/: STOP, and name the file:line and the registration shape. Do not edit src/ and do not narrow the census.</trigger>
    <trigger>4. A sweep ledger route key is not found on the branch (renamed, deleted, or already fixed by a landed 159-166 commit), or a landed fix cannot be expressed as a credit: record what you found (the commit, and the new key if it was re-keyed) and STOP for the main session's reconciliation of that entry. Do not invent a key, re-own an entry, or drop one silently.</trigger>
    <trigger>5. A credit vocabulary addition (a filter, a seam, a decision-service token or an admin mechanism) that would credit a general-purpose service rather than an authorization decision: STOP and present the choice. Also STOP for an addition that would credit any sweep route OTHER than the 16 InsufficientDecision keys listed in the ledger. The 74 NoDecision keys must stay uncredited until their fix tasks act.</trigger>
    <trigger>6. Crediting RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin") while its assertion also passes a token whose scope merely contains "admin" (AuthorizationModule.cs:371-373): record it in the note and continue with the credit as specified. If you judge the admin credit unsafe because of it, STOP and present the option of making admin credit conditional on a fixed policy (a separate task) rather than changing the policy here.</trigger>
    <trigger>7. Any UNOWNED-NEW finding you rate critical or high (GET /healthz/dataverse/doc/{id} is expected to be one): write it at the top of the task note and in current-task.md, send it to the main session if you run as a sub-agent, then continue. A live anonymous disclosure must not wait for the task to finish.</trigger>
    <trigger>8. The number of UNOWNED-NEW findings exceeds 25: STOP after classification and send the list to the main session before writing the controls, because the owner may want to re-scope the fix tasks first.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (task 074) is the only route-authorization guard. tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SessionOwnershipGuardTests.cs covers only {sessionId} routes and their body-scoped twins. A grep for other route-guard tests at authoring found none. Every new element is data or a rule inside this one guard: the credited allow-list, the attachment-form census, NonDecidingAttachments, AdminOnlyRoutes, HandlerDecision, CallerContextSeams, PermanentBasis, Gap, ObservedMechanisms and SweepFindings.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extend. The task extends the existing guard in place and creates no new guard, test project or product type. One optional partial-class file holds its data, to keep the 2289-line file cohesive and to localize the 159-166 merge conflicts.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The guard keeps reading 25 of 120 files and keeps crediting filters that decide nothing. The 82 routes the sweep found then stay invisible to the build, 17 of them critical, including cross-matter reads of analyses, events, records and RAG content. A fix that regresses passes CI, and the next sign-in-only route over an app-only client merges green. Without aggregator prefixes, a waiver for S-09 would also silently cover the external module route that produces the same fragment key. GET /healthz/dataverse/doc/{id}, an anonymous read of document metadata by id, was outside the sweep's scope and would stay unseen.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs (if the split is chosen)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-167-every-route-authorization-guard.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Census:
- A test asserts that the GovernedFiles set equals the EndpointFiles() set exactly. Every census file is classified, including Endpoints/Diagnostics/TenantContainerResolverEndpoint.cs, Endpoints/Onboarding/ConsentCallbackEndpoint.cs and Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs.
- EndpointFiles() counts a file that registers only MapMethods or MapHealthChecks.
- ExpectedEndpointFileCount stays pinned, with a history entry for this task.
- Negative: an inline fixture registering only MapMethods is counted, and a GovernedFiles entry naming a missing file fails. A seeded extra endpoint file fails naming it; use an inline fixture, or a temporary file in the test's own scan root.
- No file is classified with the retired file-level HandlerAuthorized scope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Scanner forms resolve to full keys:
- PATCH /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/context, PATCH /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId} and PATCH /api/ai/chat/sessions/{sessionId}/tabs (MapMethods with ["PATCH"]).
- GET /healthz and GET /healthz/catalog (MapHealthChecks).
- GET /api/diagnostics/tenant-container-resolver and POST /api/onboarding/consent-callback (const paths).
- Aggregator routes, for example GET /api/spe/configs/{id:guid}, GET /api/spe/containers/{containerId} (static call form), POST /api/compose/upload, GET /api/v1/external/projects/{id:guid}, POST /api/v1/external-access/grant, and all five /api/v1/external/api/dataverse/* routes.
- POST /api/compose/webhooks/spe-doc-changed resolves from the `routes` parameter with no doubled prefix.
The completeness test's independent count includes the new forms and matches the scanner for every governed file. Negative: inline fixtures with an unresolvable const path, an unknown aggregator, and a MapMethods call in an unreadable form each fail as unparseable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Duplicate keys:
- A test fails when two registrations produce the same route key. Negative: an inline fixture of ExternalModuleDataEndpoints scanned WITHOUT its aggregator binding produces "POST /api/dataverse/fetch", which collides with Api/Dataverse/FetchEndpoints.cs, and the test fails naming both files.
- ProjectClosureEndpoint.cs is NotMapped, with a test that fails if MapProjectClosureEndpoint gains a caller. The real scan produces no duplicate close-project key.
- Rule E does not flag the Compose webhook on `routes`. Negative: a fixture with an absolute "/api/..." path on the bound group parameter still fails Rule E.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rule A over every route:
- Every route of every governed file is credited (a per-resource filter, a resource policy, a verified HandlerDecision, or admin-only in AdminOnlyRoutes) or waived.
- The test name and failure text describe the every-route rule and its remedy.
- Negative: two cases each fail naming the route: a fixture copy of FileAccessEndpoints with .AddDocumentAuthorizationFilter("read") removed from a route, and a fixture route carrying only RequireAuthorization().
- Positive: these controls still pass: the four historical-miss controls, the nested-group control, the Office baseline control and the Office positive control.
- Detector_PositiveControl_DoesNotFireOnGatedRoutes is updated to the real forms .AddBulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter() and .AddEntityAccessFilter(), with a comment saying why.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Decorative forms are not credited. Inline fixture routes carrying ONLY one of the following each classify as no credit:
- .AddAnalysisRecordAuthorizationFilter();
- .AddEndpointFilter&lt;CommunicationAuthorizationFilter&gt;();
- .AddAiAuthorizationFilter() and .AddEndpointFilter&lt;AiAuthorizationFilter&gt;();
- .AddDataverseAuthorizationFilter(EntitySource.FromRouteValueWithRecord) and .AddDataverseAuthorizationFilter(EntitySource.FromFetchXmlBody);
- .AddTenantAuthorizationFilter();
- .AddEndpointFilter&lt;WorkspaceAuthorizationFilter&gt;();
- .AddAgentAuthorizationFilter(), .AddCallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter(), .AddReportingAuthorizationFilter(), .AddSpeAdminTenantScopeFilter().
Positive: .AddAnalysisExecuteAuthorizationFilter(), .AddDataverseAuthorizationFilter(EntitySource.FromRouteValue), .AddBulkDownloadAuthorizationFilter(), .AddSessionOwnershipFilter() and .AddDelegationRuleFilter() classify as per-resource credit. Fail closed: an unknown ".AddFooAuthorizationFilter()" classifies as NO credit, and it fails the attachment-form census naming file:line. An allow-list entry that no route attaches fails.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Pass-through pins:
- One test per NonDecidingAttachments entry reads the real filter source, and passes while the pass-through exists: AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs:185-212; AiAuthorizationFilter.cs:84, plus zero DocumentAnalysisRequest-bound handlers; CommunicationAuthorizationFilter.cs (whole file); DataverseAuthorizationFilter.cs:177-193; TenantAuthorizationFilter.cs:76-81; SpeAdminTenantScopeFilter.cs:76-78; and the identity-only and role-only filters.
- Each entry names its OwningTask per the constraint.
- Negative: an inline fixture of each filter, with the pass-through replaced by a decision, makes its pin fail with the "delete this entry, credit the form" remedy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rule B kept:
- NoAuthorizationFilterIsDecorative and RuleBCoversEveryFilterRuleACredits pass over the new allow-list.
- SessionOwnershipFilter.cs and DelegationRuleFilter.cs are now inspected; SessionOwnershipFilter passes through an OWNER-COMPARISON ClaimOnly reason.
- Decision tokens match whole identifiers. Negative: a fixture filter whose only token is "IAiAuthorizationServiceFactory" (or "MyAuthorizationServiceHelper") does not satisfy "AuthorizationService". Positive: AnalysisAuthorizationFilter.cs satisfies "IAiAuthorizationService".
- KnownDecorativeFilters stays empty.
- The ClaimOnlyFilters reasons for CommunicationAuthorizationFilter and AgentAuthorizationFilter no longer claim per-record scoping elsewhere, or "no document data".
- The existing Rule B negative control (the decorative SemanticSearch fixture) and the prose control still fail and pass as before.
- The note lists every filter whose Rule B verdict changed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Admin:
- Only RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin"), RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.RagApiKey), AddSpeAdminAuthorizationFilter and AddRegistrationAuthorizationFilter count as admin.
- AdminOnlyRoutes is pinned and grouped by file, with a reason per group.
- Negative: these three cases each fail: a fixture route with RequireAuthorization("SystemAdmin") that is not in the pin fails as "added"; a pinned route that gains a per-resource filter fails as "removed"; and a route credited only by AddReportingAuthorizationFilter or RequireAuthorization(AuthPolicies.ExternalCollaboration) is NOT admin, and is flagged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">HandlerDecision:
- For every declaration, the handler is located, and the seam token is found as a whole identifier, outside comments, in the declared body after following at most two declared hops.
- Hops resolve across src/server/** (a hop into src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core is resolved, not refused).
- Negative: each of these fails: a declaration whose handler body lacks the seam; a declaration naming a handler that does not exist; a seam token present only in a comment; a seam that is not in DecisionServices or CallerContextSeams; a hop naming an interface; and a hop method with two overloads of which only one contains the seam.
- Positive: GET /api/documents/{documentId}/permissions (AuthorizationService in Api/PermissionsEndpoints.cs) passes as a HandlerDecision.
- Each CallerContextSeams entry carries a reason and the seam type's file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Waiver semantics:
- Every Permanent waiver has a PermanentBasis from the closed set.
- Every Pending waiver has a Gap, and an OwningTask in {"159".."166", "UNOWNED-NEW"}.
- InsufficientDecision waivers carry ObservedMechanisms equal to the route's current authorization-relevant fingerprint.
Stale rules, each with a seeded negative:
- a NoDecision Pending waiver on a route that gains any credit (including a HandlerDecision) fails;
- an InsufficientDecision waiver whose route's fingerprint changed fails;
- adding .RequireRateLimiting to an InsufficientDecision route does NOT change its fingerprint (positive);
- a NoDecision waiver on a route that is already credited fails ("use InsufficientDecision");
- a Permanent waiver on a route that has a per-resource credit or a HandlerDecision fails as redundant;
- an AnonymousByDesign waiver on a route that is not anonymous fails;
- an anonymous route with neither an AnonymousByDesign nor a Pending waiver fails;
- any waiver on an absent route fails (the existing rule, kept).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Sweep ledger:
- SweepFindings holds exactly the 90 route keys of the 82 findings in the background, each with its S-id, severity, owning task and Gap.
- A test asserts that each entry with ResolvedBy null has a Pending waiver whose OwningTask and Gap equal the ledger's, and that no sweep route carries a Permanent waiver.
- An entry with ResolvedBy set has no waiver, passes Rule A by credit, and has a ProofTest naming a test file that exists and contains the named method.
- Negative: each of these fails: seeding a Permanent waiver on POST /api/v1/events; deleting the Pending waiver of GET /api/dataverse/record/{entityLogicalName}/{id:guid} without setting ResolvedBy; re-owning POST /api/communications/send to "166"; and setting ResolvedBy on an entry with a ProofTest naming a method that does not exist.
- The failure text tells a fix task to make the route pass by credit, delete its waiver, and set ResolvedBy to its task id and ProofTest to its deny test.</criterion>
